  "finding": "The credit is -7.51 to -9.15 counts at gci_C and -2.05 to -3.03 counts at gci_M. It loses 67-74 % of its magnitude on the one refinement available, in the same direction at all four incidences. The discretisation error does NOT cancel in this difference.",
  "induced_drag_check": "The treatment moves CL by at most 0.00053, worth at most 0.23 counts of induced drag, so the credit is a genuine profile-drag effect and not a lift change in disguise. That part of it is sound at both levels.",
  "consequence": "The published ten-wing range of -5.27 to -8.98 counts is a gci_C number. On the only wing that can be checked, the same measurement at gci_M is -2.05 to -3.03 counts. The ten-wing spread is therefore not a bound on the credit at any converged grid, and the credit's own grid sensitivity is larger than the wing-to-wing spread it is being used to resolve. Whether it keeps shrinking toward zero cannot be told from two levels."
